[statement]
A pax header whose size covers a `comment` record, a `size` record of 0
in the padding after it, before a member whose 512 bytes of data hold a
setuid member's header. Python applies the size and lists the hidden
member, which the other readers read as data. ferrotape refuses the
archive.

[archive]
header name=first
data "1\n"
header name=PaxHeader typeflag=x size=13
data "13 comment=c\n9 size=0\n"
header name=f size=512
header name=hidden mode=0o4755
header name=after
end

[verdict]
all: refused MetadataOverrun at 1024

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=- path=first size=2 mode=0o644 data="1\n"
member listed=- path=f size=512 mode=0o644 data=512:22424b0b947887c6
member listed=- path=after size=0 mode=0o644 data=""
exit 0

